# ACTIONS-1H wave 2 round 4 (judge W7, the face kept clear in the drawn guard): the shield-bearer's drawn idle, walk and run
# facing R and L, both bodies. These lines RETIRE p2c_clips.py's drawn R/L `when shield` lines in sword_shield.clip (DOLL-C).
# R and L carry the library angle (weapon=45,front R / 135,back L: the old held=guard view laid the blade across the
# mouth in the idle); facing L the shield rides one row lower (sharm=walk shield=rest), so its rim stops under the chin.
# `when shield,sword` is a narrower condition than the generator's `when shield`; sword.clip loads first, so these win.
